  "gcps22": {
    "figure": "household-map",
    "markup": "<p>Compare two periods. Choose an income or child-poverty measure, then hover, tap or select a tract for details.</p><div class=\"map-controls\"><label>Measure<select><option value=\"0\">Median household income</option><option value=\"1\" selected=\"\">Children living in poverty</option></select></label><label>Earlier period<select></select></label><label>Later period<select></select></label><label>2022–23 school zone<select><option value=\"\">No outline</option></select></label></div><div class=\"map-key\"></div><div class=\"map-panels\"></div><label class=\"tract-pick\">Explore a census tract <select></select></label><output aria-live=\"polite\"></output><small>Income uses 2024 dollars. Child poverty is the share of children under 18 for whom poverty status was determined. School outlines are for orientation. Changes are shown only for sufficiently comparable tracts.</small><noscript>&lt;p>Enable JavaScript to explore the tract maps. Countywide child poverty was 6.3% in Census 2000 and an estimated 14.7% in 2020–24.&lt;/p></noscript><div class=\"credit\">Sources: Gwinnett County, U.S. Census Bureau, BLS and school-zone GIS <sup class=\"refs\"><a href=\"#source-10\" aria-label=\"Source 10\">[10]</a><a href=\"#source-12\" aria-label=\"Source 12\">[12]</a><a href=\"#source-13\" aria-label=\"Source 13\">[13]</a><a href=\"#source-14\" aria-label=\"Source 14\">[14]</a><a href=\"#source-15\" aria-label=\"Source 15\">[15]</a><a href=\"#source-16\" aria-label=\"Source 16\">[16]</a></sup></div>"
  },
